Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> Because the bolts vanish I'd like to enchant my daggers, but I
> also want a melee weapon enchanted (and also the skill enhanced).
> Frosty seems to do most damage, so should I #enhance long swords
> to basic, what do you think? And two blessed scrolls of enchant
> weapon shall be better spent on the daggers or on Frosty?

I'd recommend the crossbow and Frost Brand.

Crossbow bolts do a suprisingly large amount of damage, you're
averaging about 25 per turn with them right now. Fully enchanted
daggers thrown with high strength will do slightly more damage but
it's not worth the weight penalty and the resources required to
enchant them. Bolts won't disappear if you ensure that they're blessed
and you have high luck, my last ranger walked into Astral carrying 70
of his starting arrows because I was able to bless and enchant them
early. 30-40 highly enchanted blessed bolts should be enough to see
you though the game.

Frost Brand is an easy choice for melee weapon. It does far more
damage than Cleaver and it's one handed so you can wear a shield of
reflection.



